,{},"kinotic-server-management",[302,642,643],{},[305,644,645],{},"localhost:58503",[302,647,648],{},"The org API and STOMP gateway the portal calls",[287,650,651,656,661],{},[302,652,653],{},[305,654,655],{},"kinotic-server-system",[302,657,658],{},[305,659,660],{},"localhost:58504",[302,662,663],{},"The API the system console and vm-manager nodes call",[287,665,666,671,676],{},[302,667,668],{},[305,669,670],{},"kinotic-server-app",[302,672,673],{},[305,674,675],{},"localhost:58505",[302,677,678,679],{},"Every application's API, each at ",[305,680,681],{},"\u003CorganizationId>--\u003CapplicationId>.apps-api.kinotic.localhost:58505",[287,683,684,689,694],{},[302,685,686],{},[305,687,688],{},"kinotic-azurite",[302,690,691],{},[305,692,693],{},"localhost:10000",[302,695,696],{},"The Azurite emulator every published UI is uploaded to, in place of the sites storage account",[287,698,699,704,709],{},[302,700,701],{},[305,702,703],{},"kinotic-sites-edge",[302,705,706],{},[305,707,708],{},"localhost:8088",[302,710,711,712,715],{},"Serves each published UI from Azurite at ",[305,713,714],{},"\u003Capp>--\u003Cui>.\u003Corg>.sites.kinotic.localhost:8088",", running the Cloudflare sites Worker itself",[287,717,718,723,728],{},[302,719,720],{},[305,721,722],{},"kinotic-gitea",[302,724,725],{},[305,726,727],{},"localhost:3001",[302,729,730,731,734,735,738],{},"The Gitea every project's repository is created on, in place of GitHub; sign in as ",[305,732,733],{},"kinotic_admin"," \u002F ",[305,736,737],{},"kinotic-gitea-admin"," to browse them",[287,740,741,744,749],{},[302,742,743],{},"Kibana",[302,745,746],{},[305,747,748],{},"localhost:5601",[302,750,751],{},"Browses Elasticsearch",[287,753,754,757,771],{},[302,755,756],{},"OpenTelemetry collector, Tempo, Loki, Mimir",[302,758,759,762,763,766,767,770],{},[305,760,761],{},"localhost:3200"," (Tempo), ",[305,764,765],{},"localhost:3100"," (Loki), ",[305,768,769],{},"localhost:9009"," (Mimir)",[302,772,773,774,777],{},"The servers' traces, logs and metrics, under the ",[305,775,776],{},"kinotic-system"," tenant",[273,779,780,781,784],{},"The stack starts with no organization: open ",[305,782,783],{},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:9090\u002Fsignup"," to create yours. To see the\nscreens filled in, add the sample data:",[409,786,788],{"className":411,"code":787,"language":413,"meta":414,"style":414},"docker compose -f compose.yml -f compose.sample-data.yml up -d\n",[305,789,790],{"__ignoreMap":414},[418,791,792,794,796,799,802,804,807,809],{"class":420,"line":421},[418,793,555],{"class":424},[418,795,558],{"class":428},[418,797,798],{"class":428}," -f",[418,800,801],{"class":428}," compose.yml",[418,803,798],{"class":428},[418,805,806],{"class":428}," compose.sample-data.yml",[418,808,561],{"class":428},[418,810,564],{"class":428},[273,812,813,814,817,818,821,822,825,826,829,830,833,834,837,838,841,842,845,846,849,850,853],{},"and sign in as ",[305,815,816],{},"kinotic@kinotic.local"," with the password ",[305,819,820],{},"kinotic",". That user belongs to the ",[305,823,824],{},"test-org","\norganization, which ",[305,827,828],{},"kinotic-sample-data",", the migration run with the ",[305,831,832],{},"fixtures"," profile, fills with\napplications, projects, members and pending invites, and ",[305,835,836],{},"kinotic-gen-schemas"," adds the ",[305,839,840],{},"ecommerce"," and\n",[305,843,844],{},"healthcare"," applications with published entity definitions and records. Pass the same ",[305,847,848],{},"-f"," files to every\nlater command on that stack, such as ",[305,851,852],{},"docker compose -f compose.yml -f compose.sample-data.yml down -v",".",[281,855,856,866],{},[284,857,858],{},[287,859,860,863],{},[290,861,862],{},"Screens with sample data",[290,864,865],{},"Screens that stay empty",[297,867,868],{},[287,869,870,879],{},[302,871,872,873,875,876,878],{},"Applications, their projects, members and settings; the organization's members and pending invites; entity definitions and their records in ",[305,874,840],{}," and ",[305,877,844],{},"; your profile",[302,880,881],{},"Deployments, and the deployment sections of the application and project overviews; jobs; observability and traces",[273,883,884,885,889,890,894],{},"The empty screens fill only from what a deployed project produces: a deployment starts when a\npush to the project's repository reaches the management server, runs as workloads on a vm-manager\nnode, and sends the telemetry the observability screens read. The compose stack hosts every\nproject's repository on its own Gitea (",[528,886,888],{"href":887},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fconfiguration#repository-host","Repository host","),\nso creating and deploying a project takes no GitHub, only a\n",[528,891,893],{"href":892},"#running-workloads-on-your-machine","vm-manager node"," to run the workloads.",[273,896,897,898,900,901,903,904,908,909,912,913,916,917,920,921,924,925,928,929,931],{},"The compose servers run the ",[305,899,511],{}," profile, which sends no email: signing up at\n",[305,902,783],{}," goes straight to naming your organization and setting a password, and\nadding a member shows the invitation's link to send on (",[528,905,907],{"href":906},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fconfiguration#demonstration-server","Demonstration server",").\nA coding agent on the same machine (Claude Code, Codex or Grok Build) connects to its MCP server at\n",[305,910,911],{},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:58503\u002Fmcp",", added beside the Kinotic plugin; ",[305,914,915],{},"deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\u002FREADME.md","\nwalks through it.\n",[305,918,919],{},"docker compose pull"," refreshes the images, and\n",[305,922,923],{},"docker compose down -v"," wipes Elasticsearch; the next ",[305,926,927],{},"up"," migrates and seeds it again.\n",[305,930,915],{}," lists the other combinations of the stack.",[404,933,935],{"id":934},"developing-kinotic","Developing Kinotic",[273,937,938,939,942],{},"Build the images of the servers you change, and the migration's when you change it, from your working\ntree. Each is tagged ",[305,940,941],{},"kinoticai\u002F\u003Cmodule>:\u003Cversion>",", the image compose runs, which it takes from your\nmachine rather than pulling it:",[409,944,946],{"className":411,"code":945,"language":413,"meta":414,"style":414},".\u002Fgradlew :kinotic-server-management:bootBuildImage :kinotic-server-system:bootBuildImage \\\n          :kinotic-server-app:bootBuildImage :kinotic-migration:bootBuildImage\ncd deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\ndocker compose up -d\n",[305,947,948,962,970,976],{"__ignoreMap":414},[418,949,950,952,955,958],{"class":420,"line":421},[418,951,425],{"class":424},[418,953,954],{"class":428}," :kinotic-server-management:bootBuildImage",[418,956,957],{"class":428}," :kinotic-server-system:bootBuildImage",[418,959,961],{"class":960},"sTEyZ"," \\\n",[418,963,964,967],{"class":420,"line":450},[418,965,966],{"class":428},"          :kinotic-server-app:bootBuildImage",[418,968,969],{"class":428}," :kinotic-migration:bootBuildImage\n",[418,971,972,974],{"class":420,"line":459},[418,973,444],{"class":443},[418,975,550],{"class":428},[418,977,979,981,983,985],{"class":420,"line":978},4,[418,980,555],{"class":424},[418,982,558],{"class":428},[418,984,561],{"class":428},[418,986,564],{"class":428},[273,988,989,990,993,994,841,996,998,999,875,1002,1005,1006,1008,1009,1012,1013,1016,1017,1020],{},"Rebuild an image and ",[305,991,992],{},"docker compose up -d"," again to replace its container. ",[305,995,619],{},[305,997,703],{}," run the ",[305,1000,1001],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-ui",[305,1003,1004],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-sites-edge"," images the CI\nbuilds with the servers; after changing ",[305,1007,633],{},", the sites Worker\n(",[305,1010,1011],{},"deployment\u002Fcloudflare\u002Fsites-worker\u002Fworker.js",") or the edge (",[305,1014,1015],{},"deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\u002Fsites-edge.ts","),\nadd ",[305,1018,1019],{},"--build"," to build them from your working tree.",[273,1022,1023],{},"Run the portal from source against the stack:",[409,1025,1027],{"className":411,"code":1026,"language":413,"meta":414,"style":414},"cd kinotic-frontend\npnpm install\npnpm dev\n",[305,1028,1029,1036,1043],{"__ignoreMap":414},[418,1030,1031,1033],{"class":420,"line":421},[418,1032,444],{"class":443},[418,1034,1035],{"class":428}," kinotic-frontend\n",[418,1037,1038,1041],{"class":420,"line":450},[418,1039,1040],{"class":424},"pnpm",[418,1042,456],{"class":428},[418,1044,1045,1047],{"class":420,"line":459},[418,1046,1040],{"class":424},[418,1048,497],{"class":428},[273,1050,1051,1052,1055,1056,1058,1059,1061,1062,1064,1065,1068,1069,1072,1073,1076,1077,1079,1080,1082,1083,853],{},"The portal on ",[305,1053,1054],{},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:5173"," calls the management server on ",[305,1057,645],{},", whose\n",[305,1060,511],{}," profile accepts its origin. The links the server\nbuilds, a sign-up's verification link or an invitation's accept link, open the portal ",[305,1063,619],{},"\nserves on ",[305,1066,1067],{},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:9090",". ",[305,1070,1071],{},"pnpm dev:system"," runs the system console on\n",[305,1074,1075],{},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:5174",", which the system server's ",[305,1078,511],{}," profile accepts too; its sign-ins\nreturn to the console ",[305,1081,619],{}," serves on ",[305,1084,1085],{},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:9091",[404,1087,1089],{"id":1088},"running-workloads-on-your-machine","Running workloads on your machine",[273,1091,1092,1093,1096,1097,1100,1101,1103,1104,1106],{},"A deployment runs its workloads on a vm-manager node. For local development that is the ",[305,1094,1095],{},"BOXLITE","\nprovider on your own machine, which runs each workload as a micro VM: macOS on Apple silicon, or\nLinux with ",[305,1098,1099],{},"\u002Fdev\u002Fkvm",". The node works beside the compose servers: the system server answers on\n",[305,1102,660],{}," and runs the ",[305,1105,511],{}," profile.",[409,1108,1110],{"className":411,"code":1109,"language":413,"meta":414,"style":414},"cd kinotic-js\u002Fworkspace\nbun install && bun run build   # the node resolves the workspace packages through their dist\ncd packages\u002Fvm-manager\nbun run dev\n",[305,1111,1112,1119,1142,1149],{"__ignoreMap":414},[418,1113,1114,1116],{"class":420,"line":421},[418,1115,444],{"class":443},[418,1117,1118],{"class":428}," kinotic-js\u002Fworkspace\n",[418,1120,1121,1123,1126,1130,1133,1135,1138],{"class":420,"line":450},[418,1122,453],{"class":424},[418,1124,1125],{"class":428}," install",[418,1127,1129],{"class":1128},"sMK4o"," &&",[418,1131,1132],{"class":424}," bun",[418,1134,464],{"class":428},[418,1136,1137],{"class":428}," build",[418,1139,1141],{"class":1140},"sHwdD","   # the node resolves the workspace packages through their dist\n",[418,1143,1144,1146],{"class":420,"line":459},[418,1145,444],{"class":443},[418,1147,1148],{"class":428}," packages\u002Fvm-manager\n",[418,1150,1151,1153,1155],{"class":420,"line":978},[418,1152,453],{"class":424},[418,1154,464],{"class":428},[418,1156,497],{"class":428},[273,1158,1159,1162,1163,1166,1167,1170,1171,1174,1175,1179,1180,1183,1184,1186,1187,841,1190,853],{},[305,1160,1161],{},".env.development",", which Bun loads for ",[305,1164,1165],{},"bun run dev",", supplies the rest: the node id\n",[305,1168,1169],{},"dev-node-1",", the SYSTEM machine identity the demonstration migration seeds, and compose's Loki\nand OTLP collector for workload logs, traces and metrics. The node registers with the system\nserver and shows ",[305,1172,1173],{},"ONLINE"," in the system console under ",[1176,1177,1178],"strong",{},"System → Worker nodes",". Guests reach\nthe org and app servers at ",[305,1181,1182],{},"192.168.127.254",", boxlite's alias for the host, which the system\nserver's ",[305,1185,511],{}," profile sets as ",[305,1188,1189],{},"kinotic.systemApi.deployment.managementServer.host",[305,1191,1192],{},"appServer.host",[273,1194,1195,1196,1199,1200,1203,1204,1207],{},"A push to a project's repository then deploys it: a sync workload checks the commit out, installs\nit and syncs its entities, and a runtime workload starts each microservice. The first deployment\npulls ",[305,1197,1198],{},"kinoticai\u002Fworkload-runner",", which takes about a minute. A workload's logs are written under\n",[305,1201,1202],{},"\u002Ftmp\u002Fkinotic-vm-logs\u002F\u003Cworkload id>"," and shipped to Loki, where the logs on a project's deployment\npage read them. A deployment that fails records why on its job run, under ",[1176,1205,1206],{},"Jobs"," in the portal.",[518,1209,1210,1241,1251],{},[521,1211,1212,1213,1216,1217,1220,1221,1224,1225,1228,1229,1232,1233,1236,1237,1240],{},"A project's UIs are published to the Azurite emulator ",[305,1214,1215],{},"compose.sites.yml"," runs, and the local\nedge beside it serves each at ",[305,1218,1219],{},"http:\u002F\u002F\u003Capp>--\u003Cui>.\u003Corg>.sites.kinotic.localhost:8088",", the URL the\nproject's deployment page links. Chrome, Edge and Firefox resolve every ",[305,1222,1223],{},"*.localhost"," name to\nthis machine; a client that does not needs the hostname in its hosts file. The sites and the\napplication API hosts (",[305,1226,1227],{},"\u003Corg>--\u003Capp>.apps-api.kinotic.localhost:58505",") are both under\n",[305,1230,1231],{},"kinotic.localhost",", so a browser treats a site and its application's API as one site and sends\nthe ",[305,1234,1235],{},"SameSite=Lax"," session cookie between them, as it does under ",[305,1238,1239],{},"kinotic.ai"," in production.",[521,1242,1243,1244,1247,1248,853],{},"The node keeps its image cache in ",[305,1245,1246],{},"~\u002F.boxlite",", which one process can hold at a time: stop the\nnode before running the vm-manager tests, or give the tests their own ",[305,1249,1250],{},"BOXLITE_HOME",[521,1252,1253],{},"The sample data's worker nodes are marked unreachable on the system server's first\nheartbeat pass, so deployments land on your node.",[269,1255,1257],{"id":1256},"testing","Testing",[404,1259,1261],{"id":1260},"javakotlin","Java\u002FKotlin",[409,1263,1265],{"className":411,"code":1264,"language":413,"meta":414,"style":414},".\u002Fgradlew test\n",[305,1266,1267],{"__ignoreMap":414},[418,1268,1269,1271],{"class":420,"line":421},[418,1270,425],{"class":424},[418,1272,1273],{"class":428}," test\n",[404,1275,1277],{"id":1276},"typescript-vitest","TypeScript (Vitest)",[409,1279,1281],{"className":411,"code":1280,"language":413,"meta":414,"style":414},"cd kinotic-js\nbun test\n",[305,1282,1283,1289],{"__ignoreMap":414},[418,1284,1285,1287],{"class":420,"line":421},[418,1286,444],{"class":443},[418,1288,447],{"class":428},[418,1290,1291,1293],{"class":420,"line":450},[418,1292,453],{"class":424},[418,1294,1273],{"class":428},[269,1296,1298],{"id":1297},"submitting-changes","Submitting Changes",[1300,1301,1302,1308,1311,1314,1320],"ol",{},[521,1303,1304,1305],{},"Fork the repository and create a feature branch from ",[305,1306,1307],{},"develop",[521,1309,1310],{},"Make your changes with clear, descriptive commit messages",[521,1312,1313],{},"Ensure all tests pass before submitting",[521,1315,1316,1317,1319],{},"Submit a pull request against the ",[305,1318,1307],{}," branch",[521,1321,1322,1323,1328,1329],{},"Accept the ",[528,1324,1327],{"href":1325,"rel":1326},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fkinotic-ai\u002Fkinotic\u002Fblob\u002Fdevelop\u002FCLA.md",[532],"Contributor License Agreement","\non your first pull request by commenting ",[305,1330,1331],{},"I have read the Kinotic CLA Document and I hereby sign the CLA",[269,1333,1335],{"id":1334},"licensing","Licensing",[273,1337,1338,1339,348,1341,348,1344,348,1347,1350,1351,875,1354,1357,1358,1361,1362,1365,1366,1373,1374,1377,1378,1385,1386,1389,1390,1393,1394,1068,1397,1399],{},"Kinotic RPC (",[305,1340,307],{},[305,1342,1343],{},"kinotic-api-gateway\u002F",[305,1345,1346],{},"kinotic-client\u002F",[305,1348,1349],{},"kinotic-idl\u002F",", and the ",[305,1352,1353],{},"core",[305,1355,1356],{},"idl","\npackages in ",[305,1359,1360],{},"kinotic-js\u002Fworkspace\u002Fpackages\u002F",") is licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and none of\nits modules may depend on a module outside it: the build fails if one declares a project dependency on such a\nmodule. Every file in a Java package with an ",[305,1363,1364],{},"ee"," segment is an Enterprise Implementation,\nlicensed under the Kinotic Enterprise License\n(",[528,1367,1370],{"href":1368,"rel":1369},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fkinotic-ai\u002Fkinotic\u002Fblob\u002Fdevelop\u002FLICENSE-ENTERPRISE",[532],[305,1371,1372],{},"LICENSE-ENTERPRISE","),\nexcept an Enterprise Extension Point: an interface, abstract class or annotation in such a package,\nsuch as ",[305,1375,1376],{},"org.kinotic.domain.api.ee.services.SecretStorageBackend",". Everything else is licensed\nunder the Elastic License 2.0 with the Kinotic Additional Limitations. The root\n",[528,1379,1382],{"href":1380,"rel":1381},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fkinotic-ai\u002Fkinotic\u002Fblob\u002Fdevelop\u002FLICENSE.md",[532],[305,1383,1384],{},"LICENSE.md"," routes each part of\nthe repository to its license. An Enterprise Feature's classes live in the ",[305,1387,1388],{},"internal\u002Fapi\u002Fee\u002F","\ntree of the module the feature belongs to, such as ",[305,1391,1392],{},"EnterpriseIdentityProviders"," in\n",[305,1395,1396],{},"kinotic-domain",[528,1398,259],{"href":260}," describes what production use\nof them requires.",[273,1401,1402],{},"The CLA grants Minds Ignited the right to license your contribution under any of these licenses,\nincluding as part of an Enterprise Feature; you keep the copyright in it.",[1404,1405,1406],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html .light .shiki 